Improved: IBTK::LDataManager::spread() and IBAMR::IMPMethod::spreadForce() spread each marker once into cell-centered and side-centered data and sum the values in ghost cells into the patches that own them. Force spread across periodic boundaries is no longer dropped, force spread outside physical boundaries is folded back into the domain by the transpose of the boundary fill, and IBTK::LDataManager::spread() requires data whose ghost cell width holds the support of the kernel. IBAMR::IBFEMethod and IBAMR::IBFESurfaceMethod now apply the transpose of the boundary fill within the accumulation of ghost values. IBAMR::IBMethod and IBAMR::IMPMethod read the input key <code>accumulate_active_patches_only</code> (default TRUE), which restricts the accumulation to the patches that hold points.
<br>
(Boyce Griffith, 2026/10/06)
